Z||000000||Thor||08-01-2000||12:59 AM||||I had a problem with my 86 GT where I would blow the 20 watt parking fuse every time I actuated the headlights. THANKS TO THIS FANTASTIC SITE I had four responses within a day! The easyest suggestion that seemed to make sence was to remove all my tail,running and turning signal bulbs from there sockets,activate the parking light switch and see if I blew the fuse[IT DIDN'T]. Then all I had to do was replace each bulb one at a time. Low and behold when I replaced one of the brake light bulbs it didn't actually blow the fuse but there was definatlly a short. If I left that bulb out my lighting system worked fine...THANKS AGAIN TO ALL FOR HELPING ME WITH MY FIERO PROBLEMS!!!    ||||reg||6
